From: Matthew Dowell <mbd06b+github@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:20:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] fix: ls-remote names its remote only after it answered,
 password redacted

Re-review FIX FIRST item 3. The `From <url>` line printed
`url.to_bstring()`, which includes a password embedded in the URL, and it
was printed before connecting, so it appeared even when the connection
failed (Git prints no `From` line then).

`from_line()` now formats the URL through its `Display`, which shows a
password as `redacted`, and the line is written only after the ref
advertisement was received. Unit test `the_from_line_never_shows_a_password`
(fails on a `to_bstring()` stub); journey
`ls_remote_names_the_default_remote_only_after_it_answered_and_without_its_password`:
an unreachable default remote prints no `From` line (fails on e534083f0's
binary), and a default remote URL `http://user:secret@127.0.0.1:1/...`
never shows `secret` on stderr.

